# Server Environment Variables

This file contains example environment variables required for the Node.js backend.
Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the appropriate values.

---

# Core Application Settings

# The port the Express server will listen on.
PORT=5000

# The base URL for the shortener service. This is used to construct the full short URL.
# Example: If your service is hosted at `https://yourshortener.com`, set this to that URL.
# Ensure it includes the protocol (http/https) and does NOT end with a slash.
BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000

---

# Database Configuration

# MongoDB connection URI.
# Replace `<username>`, `<password>`, `<cluster-url>`, and `<database-name>` with your actual MongoDB credentials.
# Example for a local MongoDB instance: mongodb://localhost:27017/urlshortener
# Example for MongoDB Atlas: mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@<cluster-url>/<database-name>?retryWrites=true&w=majority
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/urlshortener_db

---

# Cross-Service Integration (Microservice Context)

# Base URL for the Real-time Weather Dashboard API.
# This could be used if the URL shortener needed to log events to a weather-related service
# or provide short links to specific weather forecasts.
WEATHER_DASHBOARD_API_URL=http://localhost:3001/api/weather

# Base URL for the Interactive E-commerce Product Catalog service.
# Useful if the shortener needs to generate short links for product pages or promotions,
# or interact with the catalog for product data.
ECOMMERCE_CATALOG_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:3002/api/products

# API Key for the AI-Powered Content Assistant.
# This could be used if the shortener needed to leverage AI for generating short link descriptions,
# analyzing link content, or integrating with content generation workflows.
AI_ASSISTANT_API_KEY=your_ai_assistant_api_key_here
AI_ASSISTANT_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:3003/api/assistant